Description
Are you a passionate Data Analyst looking for an exciting opportunity to grow and work on impactful projects? We are seeking a highly motivated Data Analyst (with reporting skills) to join our dynamic team. You'll have the flexibility to work fully remotely. As a key member of our dynamic organization, you will be responsible for gathering, analyzing, and presenting data to support informed decision-making and drive operational excellence. This role offers an exciting opportunity to work on diverse projects and collaborate with cross-functional teams in a fast-paced environment.
What You'll Do:

Develop and maintain robust data analysis and reporting systems to track key performance indicators (KPIs), trends, and metrics;


Collaborate closely with stakeholders to gather data requirements and ensure alignment with business objectives;
Conduct in-depth analysis of data to uncover insights and trends, and provide actionable recommendations to stakeholders;
Continuously improve reporting processes and systems to enhance efficiency, accuracy, and usability;
Stay informed about industry trends and best practices in reporting, data analysis, and business intelligence.

 Requirements

Bachelor's degree in Business Administration, Finance, Statistics, or a related field;


Minimum of 3 years of experience in data analysis, reporting, or business intelligence roles;
Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Excel, including pivot tables, formulas, power queries, and power pivots;
Experience in data visualization tools is an asset;
Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with a keen attention to detail;
Excellent communication skills, with the ability to convey complex information clearly and concisely;
Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a multicultural environment;
Fluency in English is required.

Benefits
We believe in rewarding talent and dedication. Here's what you can expect as part of our team:

Competitive full-time salary;
Private Health Coverage on the Company’s group program;
Flexible Working Hours;
Top-of-the-Line Tools;
Professional Development: Benefit from language courses, specialized training, and continuous learning opportunities;
Career Growth: Work with some of the most innovative and exciting specialists in the industry;
Dynamic Work Environment: Thrive in a setting that offers challenging goals, autonomy, and mentoring, fostering both personal and company growth.

If you want an exciting challenge, work with some of the coolest technologies, and enjoy your time doing it, then join us! Submit your detailed CV in English, quoting reference: (DAR/09/24).
You may also consider all our other open vacancies by visiting the career section of our website (www.eurodyn.com) and follow us on Twitter (@EURODYN_Careers) and LinkedIn.
