Description
Join our dynamic team at EUROPEAN DYNAMICS as a Junior FP&A Analyst and play a crucial role in supporting financial planning, analysis, and reporting activities. Working closely with various stakeholders, you will provide valuable insights and recommendations to drive informed decision-making and optimize financial performance. This is your chance to contribute to the success of a growing organization and advance your career in a collaborative and innovative environment.
What You'll Do:

Assist in the development and maintenance of financial models, forecasts, and budgets to support strategic planning and decision-making processes;
Assist in variance analysis and performance reporting to assess financial performance against targets and identify key drivers of performance;
Support month-end and year-end close processes, ensuring accuracy and completeness of financial data;
Collaborate with cross-functional teams to understand business needs, trends, and opportunities, and provide financial guidance and support;
Support improvement initiatives to enhance financial processes, systems, and reporting capabilities.

Requirements


Bachelor's degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics, or a related field;
1-2 years of experience in financial analysis, or related roles, will be considered a plus;
Strong analytical skills with the ability to interpret complex financial data and trends;
Experience in financial modeling, forecasting, and budgeting, will be considered an asset;
Fluency in English;
Excellent communication and presentation skills;
Detail-oriented with a commitment to accuracy and integrity;
Advanced proficiency in Excel;
Ability to thrive in a fast-paced environment and manage multiple priorities effectively.



Benefits

We believe in rewarding talent and dedication. Here's what you can expect as part of our team:

Competitive full-time salary;
Private Health Coverage on the Company’s group program;
Flexible Working Hours;
Top-of-the-Line Tools;
